      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 569347097,
          "type": null,
          "body": "That will surely suffice as a workaround, it's a bit unfortunate but anyway, I'm not opposed at all.\n\nBut maybe consider these two alternatives:\n* Use a STATIC \"qtui\" library instead of an OBJECT library.\n* Add a CMake warning for the buggy CMake versions and assume users are using the latest CMake bugfix release for their particular minor version. Even glacial distros like Debian and RHEL run the latest bugfix release, no? They should anyway.\n\nThanks for working on this by the way. Glad the spurious MOC/whatever runs are being eliminated.",
